  "summary_en": "Ghana's binding civil aviation directive regulating remotely piloted aircraft systems (drones). It sets registration, permits, operator certification, pilot licensing, airworthiness, safety management, BVLOS, detect-and-avoid, C2 link loss, security and enforcement rules, with implementing standards, to integrate RPAS safely into Ghanaian airspace.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Commercial RPAS operation requires an RPAS Operator Certificate; all RPAS must be registered and hold a permit, renewed annually.",
   "Weight classes: small (≤1.5 kg), light (≤7 kg), large (>7 kg); large RPAS require special airworthiness certificate.",
   "Altitude limit of 400 ft, 5–10 km exclusion around airports, 30 m from people/buildings, night ops need authorisation.",
   "Operators must have an approved SMS, emergency plan, incident reporting, and BVLOS requires detect-and-avoid and C2 link-loss procedures.",
   "BVLOS Category C (waypoint control) not accepted; remote pilots need licence, Class III medical, age 18+."
  ],
